        "created_at": "2024-05-21T23:10:05Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-05-21T23:10:05Z",
        "body": "> The maximally consistent interpretation is to say that initializer RHSes are basically new function bodies and therefore should unset the yield/await flags, but we could also just unconditionally ban them. We do that for await in static blocks (by unconditionally setting the flags and then having an early error for \"contains await\").\r\n\r\nAgreed. I think these should all be [~Yield, +Await, ~Return] with Early Error ban for `await`, like `static` blocks.",
        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "pin": null,
        "reactions": {
